  "core_idea": "Students' choices, effort and persistence depend on two things: whether they expect to succeed and how much they value the task. Value has four parts: interest, importance to identity, usefulness and cost.",
  "key_concepts_note": "Use the concepts already stored for this theory in the library (theories.concepts).",
  "when_to_use": [
    "Why do students choose or drop subjects such as STEM?",
    "How do parents, teachers or culture shape students' expectancies and values?",
    "Typical data: surveys, longitudinal studies, interviews."
  ],
  "common_mistakes": [
    "Measuring 'motivation' as one score instead of separate expectancy and value.",
    "Leaving out cost, which recent work treats as a separate dimension.",
    "Confusing expectancy (can I do this task?) with general self-esteem."
  ],
